WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.940
Hey YouTubers, It's Charlie. Happy Super Bowl Sunday.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.840
So we're ganna be getting a whole bunch of stuff today.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.620
But I wanted to start with Deadpool and Ryan Reynolds.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.640
Because he just said he wants to play Deadpool for the rest of time.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.940
So What does that mean?

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.980
Most of you have probably learned to take what Hollywood actors say with a grain of salt,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.760
But all this means is that they're definitely going to be working on a sequel.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.380
Deadpool is tracking for big box office,

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.460
it was a relatively cheap movie to make as far as big superhero movies go,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.980
Think about X-Men Apocalypse;

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.100
They have probably spent twice- maybe three times as much making that movie

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.020
and marketing it.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.800
People are SO crazy to see Deadpool that Fox is actually spending more marketing the movie

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.720
then they spent to make it. That's how excited they are about it.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:45.040
And usually that's a pretty good sign that they're ganna greenlight a sequel.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.540
What would that sequel be?

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.680
Well, the first logical sequel would be Deadpool and Cable.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.820
The first time Deadpool met Cable was the first time Deadpool appeared in the comics,

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.680
during New Mutants number 98.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.440
Deadpool was hired to kill Cable

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.680
So logically they would do a version of that in the comics

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.760
Obviously they have a long relationship, they haven't always been at each others throats,

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.240
So the first time they appear on camera together

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.560
they would probably fight a little, then eventually they'd start working together.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.880
So even if they decide to do a Deadpool vs Wolverine movie first

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:20.480
They can still include Easter Eggs for the first time Deadpool was hired to kill Cable,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.000
before the story takes whatever direction they want the movie to take.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.920
It's like Batman v. Superman,

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.520
They're ganna fight each other at first,

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.600
then they're ganna be friends and form the Justice League.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.900
It's kinda the same thing with Deadpool and Cable.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.260
And Deadpool and Wolverine.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.940
Although when Cable and Wolverine are forced to work together with Deadpool

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:38.480
it's ALWAYS begrudgingly, they ALWAYS hate the shit out of him.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.180
He's just the guy that wont shut up, the bugs-bunny character.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.080
What a lot of people are quoting of the movie.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.820
There have been advanced screenings, so people are starting to review it.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:47.480
Of course, everybody loves it.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.300
It's to be expected, it's ganna be a lot of fun,

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:52.800
But the other key issue that you guys need to check out if you haven't read it in a while,

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.000
It might be on Marvel Unlimited,

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.380
is Wolverine number 88 from volume 2

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:00.500
That's the first time Deadpool met Wolverine.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:05.320
The title of that story, total bugs-bunny, 'It D-D-D Deadpool Folks'.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:10.980
They meet because Wolverine goes to check on his friend, who's living with CopyCat- Deadpool's x-girlfriend.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:14.960
He finds that Deadpool came back to try and get CopyCat back

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:18.820
but ended up trashing her place, so Wolverine gets pissed, they fight

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:21.900
and he gets even more pissed when he can't wound Deadpool

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.640
because of his healing factor.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.580
So like the bug-bunny title implies

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:31.380
it's a total Loony Toons story, with Elmer Fudd- Wolverine trying to kill bug-bunny - Deadpool.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:35.240
I love the idea of Elmer Fudd- Wolverine, that's just so beautiful.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.080
Hugh Jackman would have so much fun.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.800
A lot of you might have noticed that he and Ryan Rynolds are really good friends

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.400
They've been taking pictures together.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.000
I think Fox is really happy about that.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.080
I don't know if necessarily that Deadpool vs Wolverine would be the next Deadpool movie,

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.140
but it's totally possible.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.880
It depends on how much longer Hugh Jackman wants to be Wolverine.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.300
Now he could change his mind too.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:57.400
Like I said, you learn to take what Hollywood actors say with a grain of salt.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:01.740
Robert Downey jr. originally was going to quite being Iron Man at a certain point.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:05.440
He was like "okay, I'm a little too old for this, so I'm ganna pass on the mantle on

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.520
to the next actor that Marvel wants to cast."

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.460
But why do actors like that decide to stick around?

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:15.960
Mostly because the studio treats them really well, the fans love it, and the movies are successful.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.660
If the movies tank, then they'll probably be like "okay, no one wants to see me do this again.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:20.600
So I'll move on."

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.680
So I think Ryan Rynolds, seeing how CRAZY people are going for Deadpool

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.200
has really jazzed him up.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.580
Seriously, a lot of the love that you guys are feeding him is repairing the damage that Green Lantern did.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:35.520
Even though actors get paid millions and millions of dollars, they still take it really personally

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.800
when people hate characters that they play.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.020
Big big characters.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:42.740
there's this story Chris Harswick told about George Clooney at ComicCon one year.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:46.340
It was many many years after George Clooney had been Batman.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.340
But Chris Hardwick said he made a little joke about Batman and Bat-nipples and

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.720
and George Clooney was like "Look dude, I just want to say that I'm sorry.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:56.820
I get it, that movie was terrible. I just want to apologize  for ruining that character"

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.460
Obviously its not all his fault that that movie was terrible

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:04.660
But it just reminds you that even really powerful, really rich actors take it really personally

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.120
when people hate the stuff that they do.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.160
So on the flip side of that, I feel like this Deadpool experience has made Ryan Rynolds

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:14.580
feel like he's 15 and just had sex for the first time again.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:17.120
So he's just like "hell yeah I want to do this again!"

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.500
and the reason I'm talking about Wolverine and Cable so much

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:22.660
for the sequel is just because the associated with the film; the director

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:26.320
the producers, the actors have been mostly talking about those characters.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:29.000
Cable was one of the first people they mention because Tim Miller was just like

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.300
"I feel like people would assassinate me if I didn't put Cable in the sequel."

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:35.360
and then everyone was like, "wait a minuet, you said sequel. Does that mean

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:36.600
that you're actually doing a sequel?"

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.160
Then Ryan Rynolds was like, "Hey, yeah, I totally want to play Deadpool forever."

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:42.300
So it's like, ok, yeah, we're probably ganna see Cable.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.800
So I'm wondering if Cable is going to be in one of the post-credit scenes.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.120
Now in all the advanced screenings that they did,

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.420
They actually kept some of the scenes out.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:52.000
So there are a couple new post-credit scenes.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.200
So whatever those are, we wont see them until the movie drops next week.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.480
So I'm thinking of the two post-credit scenes;

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.260
One is Deadpool specific, it's ganna be like, Cable or something like that

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.800
and the other is X-Men specific.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.120
Because this is part of the X-Men universe.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.480
So we'll probably get a funny Deadpool post credit scene

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:10.920
where he breaks the fourth wall and does something with X-Men chacters

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:13.960
then we'll get a world building post-credits scene.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:19.340
Where it's like: holy shit it's Cable. Holy shit it's him with characters we're ganna see in his sequel.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.560
And no idea when they would drop a sequel if that actually ends up coming.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:25.380
They'll probably wait to announce that till a little bit after the movie comes out.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:28.500
If it does crazy insane they'll probably try and fast track it.

